      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792819504672,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Check whether the tree is empty or not .\n\n2. If it is empty print tree is empty .\n\n3. If it is not empty set the pointer to the root node .\n\n4. Push the current node in the stack \n\n5. Also push its right child by making its address negative .\n\n6. Move towards left .\n\n7. Repeat the step 4 to 6 untill you get null .\n\n8. When you get null check whether the stack is empty or not .\n\n9. If stack is empty finish and return .\n\n10. If stack is not empty :\n\n a. Pop the top node form stack .\n b. if it is positive then print it and goto step 8 .\n c. if it is negative make it positive and goto step 4 .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Check whether the tree is empty or not .\n\n2. If it is empty print tree is empty .\n\n3. If it is not empty set the pointer to the root node .\n\n4. Push the current node in the stack \n\n5. Also push its right child by making its address negative .\n\n6. Move towards left .\n\n7. Repeat the step 4 to 6 untill you get null .\n\n8. When you get null check whether the stack is empty or not .\n\n9. If stack is empty finish and return .\n\n10. If stack is not empty :\n\n a. Pop the top node form stack .\n b. if it is positive then print it and goto step 8 .\n c. if it is negative make it positive and goto step 4 .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
